    "categoryId": "riq-cat-technology",
    "headline": "Have you ever tried to get that perfect top down shot of a product or stream a crafting session and you couldn't get the camera just right? Tabletop mounts can get in the way and mini tripods can be unstable. The best solution I've found so far is this sturdy, articulating boom arm that secures to any desk with the adjustable clamp.",
    "description": "Have you ever tried to get that perfect top down shot of a product or stream a crafting session and you couldn't get the camera just right? Tabletop mounts can get in the way and mini tripods can be unstable. The best solution I've found so far is this sturdy, articulating boom arm that secures to any desk with the adjustable clamp. Image from Amazon The VIJIM LS08 Flexible Overhead Camera Mount Desk Stand can extend far over any table so you can master your top down shots or create an angle for cooking videos, crafting, or unboxing. The ball joints are easy to tighten and allow you to move the arm at any angle, at 2 different joints. I was able to mount a phone or small mirrorless camera but it's made for microphones or cameras, or anything that threads onto a 1/4 or 3/8 thread mount. Both threaded adapters are included and screw on to the end of the boom arm. Flexibility Each ballhead can move fluidly around the joints. There's plenty of clearance to mount the arm on a desk, with 5cm of clearance. Stable The boom arm can rest at 90 degrees, holding a small DSLR or mirrorless camera with ease. Gain reach with your mic and tuck it away when not in use. Perfect the shot Make unboxing or cooking videos more professional by elevating your camera overead and capturing the perfect angle for your audience. I've used many boom arms and they can be limiting if you only have one elbow joint, I love this one because it has 2. You can make it taller, extend it further, or create a unique angle with the dual ballhead design. This one is a keeper.",
