    "headline": "The go to, do all, charge everything almost infinitely...brick.",
    "description": "The go to, do all, charge everything almost infinitely...brick. This large-capacity brick is my new main squeeze for the backpack. I'm always on the go, and this thing will keep all the devices powered all day. The shell is sturdy and rugged, with a textured grip on the red side and smooth glass on the top. It has a display that shows the charge level, which has become a new staple requirement for me when purchasing power banks. You never want to get somewhere and then worry about whether you charged up your brick. It features (2) USB A ports, (1) USB Micro port, and (1) USB C. The USB-C is bi-directional, so you'll want to use that as the main charging port when powering this up for the day. I would prefer this to have 2 USB-C ports, rather than 2 A ports, but it's going to work for my day either way. USB-C is just a faster way to charge so it's always my preferred method Ultra-High Capacity 50000mAh Portable Charger for a Week: The 50000mAh power bank can charge an iPhone 15 up to 12 times and a Samsung S22 up to 13.5 times 22.5W max output and 18W input PD 4.0 and QC 4.0 charging protocols Multiple ports and types High precision LED display Weights 18.72 oz (a bit heavy) and measures 1.3 x 2.9 x 6.1 in The Bextoo portable charger power bank is a solid deal at 29.99. As of writing this article, it is on sale for 23.96 USD on Prime. This item has a large capacity and is easy to take in any bag. It comes with a USB-C charging cable to power it up, and it can also be used to power the latest phones and gadgets with USB-C ports. The digital screen is easy to read and will let you know just how full the bank is. This is a solid pick for anyone. Click the image below for the direct link. Written on May 17, 2025",
